  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council; \"the elections take place on January 15th\". Nominations were received in the Tontine on Monday 6 January (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1908, p. 5). Each party nominated only for the ward it held, and \"in Armagh all the candidates nominated have been returned unopposed, which leaves the representation unchanged\". No Unionist papers were handed in for this ward (the South Ward of 1905 and 1911). Philip Lavery is styled J.P."
